# Author order here is the BOOK's, not the paper's. Sean Davis conceived the
# book and wrote most chapters, so he leads. The F1000 article uses a
# senior-last order (Shepherd Kern, Davis) -- a different convention for a
# different artifact. Do not "sync" one to the other.
abstract: >-
  A collection of chapters teaching introductory R, statistics, and
  Bioconductor for biologists and others coming to data science for the
  first time. Original content (prose, original figures, and example code)
  is licensed CC-BY 4.0. Some third-party figures, datasets, and adapted
  passages retain their own licenses; each is listed, with its license, on
  the book's Contributors & acknowledgments page.
keywords:
  - R
  - Bioconductor
  - statistics
  - data science
  - genomics
  - teaching
license: CC-BY-4.0
url: "https://seandavi.github.io/RBiocBook"
repository-code: "https://github.com/seandavi/RBiocBook"
version: "2026.08.06"
date-released: "2026-08-06"
# Concept DOI -- always resolves to the latest version. Keep it as the concept
# DOI rather than a version DOI so citations stay valid across releases.
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.20574829"
